.TH MD_GET_FREQUENCY 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.3.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_get_frequency \- query the current channel frequency
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

float md_get_frequency(const morsedec_decoder_t *decoder);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Query the current channel frequency.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the current channel frequency in Hz, or -1 for NULL decoder or no
current channel. This query has no errno-based failure return.
.SH REMARKS
The result is a measured FFT-bin center. For I/Q this is a signed offset
relative to 0 Hz IF, with no RF center frequency added. Since -1 Hz can be a
valid I/Q result, test md_get_state()!=MORSEDEC_STATE_NONE or use channel
enumeration to distinguish an absent selection. The scalar getter does not
report all carriers.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0.
Version 0.3.0 uses the float API and shared-library ABI 2.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_get_state (3),
.BR md_get_channel (3),
.BR md_pin_frequency (3)
